355	// ===========================================================================
356	// History layer: HealthSample snapshots, uptime math, and StatusIncident state
357	//
358	// The four probes above are INSTANTANEOUS — they say what is true right now and
359	// keep no memory. Everything below turns that into history: the worker monitor
360	// calls sampleHealth() on its cadence to persist one HealthSample per component,
361	// and the readers compute uptime %, a bucketed timeline, and open/resolved
362	// incidents from those rows. All the arithmetic is factored into PURE functions
363	// (uptimeFromSamples / bucketTimeline / decideIncident) so it is unit-testable
364	// with an injected clock and injected samples, no DB required.
365	// ===========================================================================
